    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/E66B3C1689D7CACD88837E5AD889588C/jobs/892497": {
      "title": "Faculty Position for Occupational Therapy",
      "description": "Faculty Position for Occupational Therapy You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Faculty Position for Occupational Therapy Hattiesburg - Hattiesburg, MS 39401 Apply Apply Description Job Summary Under the supervision of the Director of Occupational Therapy, the faculty member performs teaching, service, and research duties in the occupational therapy field. Duties and Responsibilities This job description does not state or imply that these are the only duties to be performed by the employee occupying this position. The duties and responsibilities listed are essential job functions and exclude functions that are incidental to the performance of fundamental job duties. Assist the university in implementing the Statement of Purpose Assist the university and department in implementing long-range institutional and financial plans Maintain standards of the profession, including rules and regulations of licensing and certification. Assist with recruitment and admissions processes for the Department of Occupational Therapy Provide academic advising for current and potential MOT students Ensure each student has met health and academic requirements for attendance at each fieldwork education experience Use active learning strategies to teach entry-level Master of Occupational Therapy learners in faculty member’s area of expertise and provide evaluation of student learning. Engage in service to the university and the profession through committee appointments, providing continuing education offerings, clinical practice, consulting, etc. Demonstrate knowledge of curriculum design with regard to principles of diversity, equity, inclusion, and justice in accordance with meeting accreditation standards. Responsible for mentoring students on scholarly projects. Demonstrate ongoing scholarly achievement and research expertise. Qualifications Required Qualifications Must hold a minimum of a master’s degree awarded by an institution accredited by a USDE-recognized regional accrediting body. Must have at least two years of clinical practice experience as an occupational therapist Must have demonstrated clinical expertise in specific area of instruction Must hold an unencumbered occupational therapy license in Mississippi Must hold a national board certification from NBCOT. Must be, or be willing to become a member of the Mississippi Occupational Therapy Association (MSOTA). Must be a member of the American Occupational Therapy Association (AOTA). Preferred Qualifications Doctor of Occupational Therapy (OTD) Have documented scholarship and research. Have knowledge of curriculum and instructional design to meet the mission and vision of the program Have two or more years of academic or clinical teaching experience. Physical Demands Must possess mobility to work in a standard classroom, lab, or office setting and to use standard office equipment, including a computer Must have vision to read printed materials and a computer screen; hearing and speech to communicate in person and over the telephone Must have the ability to sit or stand for extended periods of time Must have strength and agility to move files, paper boxes, and minor office equipment Must be able to maintain office hours and perform duties in an on-campus setting Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/E66B3C1689D7CACD88837E5AD889588C/jobs/931229": {
      "title": "HVAC Specialist and Building Mechanic",
      "description": "HVAC Specialist and Building Mechanic You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account HVAC Specialist and Building Mechanic Hattiesburg - Hattiesburg, MS 39401 Apply Apply Description Job Summary Under the direction of the Facilities Manager, the HVAC Specialist performs skilled work in the installation, maintenance, troubleshooting, and repair of heating, ventilation, air conditioning, and related mechanical systems. The position is responsible for helping maintain a safe, efficient, and comfortable indoor environment for students, faculty, staff, and visitors across university facilities. Responsibilities include performing preventive maintenance, responding to service requests and equipment failures, participating in a rotating on-call schedule for campus emergencies, assisting with general building maintenance, and supporting campus events as needed. The HVAC Specialist also collaborates with other Facilities Management staff to ensure the reliable operation and upkeep of university buildings and infrastructure. Duties and Responsibilities This job description does not state or imply that these are the only duties to be performed by the employee occupying this position.  Duties and responsibilities listed are essential job functions and exclude functions which are incidental to the performance of fundamental job duties. Assist the university in implementing the statement of purpose . Assist the university in implementing the long-range institutional plan. Plan, organize and supervise all WCC HVAC operations. Inspect, repair, maintain, troubleshoot, adjust and regulate heating, ventilation, refrigeration and air conditioning equipment including heat pumps, heating and ventilating units, air conditioning with gas or electric heat, reciprocating chillers, multi-zone units, hot water heating boilers, cooling towers, thermal energy storage systems, pumps, air handlers, return and exhaust fans, air compressors, variable air volume systems, refrigerators, and ice makers. Replace valves, fans, motors, gaskets, filters and belts; refrigerant oil, contractors, fuses, compressors, capacitors, bearings, sheaves, actuators; use various testing devices to locate defective parts, pump down units with vacuum pump; use welding equipment to repair refrigeration lines; adjust RPM on motors and fans; check and adjust gas pressure on heating units. Adjust and install switches, gauges, thermostats, valves, tubing and other parts as needed; makes pipe connections and repairs; troubleshoots and repairs electrical components pertaining to heating, ventilating and air conditioning equipment. Check and test new equipment before installation; calibrate pneumatic and electrical controls; calibrates repairs and replaces thermostats; adjust, balance and redesign air flow through ducts, diffusers, and registers; sets time clocks for heating, ventilating and air conditioning equipment; maintain chemical water treatment for cooling towers, hot and cold water systems and thermal energy storage systems; operate and adjust building electronic controls for temperature and scheduling control; initiate and implement preventive maintenance system. Keep up to date with regard to new regulations and procedures pertaining to heating, ventilation, air conditioning and refrigeration. Makes estimates of labor and material costs for job; research catalogs to locate materials and parts required for jobs; requisitions, receives and stores parts and materials; purchases parts and material on open Purchase Orders; maintains records of time and materials. Assigns and checks the work of helpers assigned to specific projects; works from blueprints, schematics and rough sketches; plans and lays out work on assigned work orders; makes rough sketches and working drawings. Cares for and stores tools and provides for security of tools, materials and equipment at the work site; assists other maintenance personnel by performing unskilled or semi-skilled duties; operate vehicles. Operate the building controls energy management system. Develop and implement a preventive maintenance program for HVAC equipment. Coordinate and supervise all HVAC related contractors. Assist with facility maintenance or repairs on occasion. Perform other job related duties as assigned. Must be able to perform duties in an on-campus setting. Qualifications Required Qualifications 5 years minimum directly related experience in the heating, ventilation and air conditioning field, with two years’ experience in a supervisory position. Valid US driver license and a clean driving history, fork Lift operator’s certificate, EPA Certified Freon gas Handlers Certificate. Ability to perform advanced math calculations Ability to read, write and speak the English language fluently. Preferred Qualifications High School diploma desirable. Physical Demands Heavy physical labor with constant standing and walking for extended periods of time; walking over rough or uneven surfaces; frequent lifting, carrying, pushing and pulling of objects weighing up to fifty (50) pounds; frequent bending, kneeling and stooping; climb and descend ladders, manual dexterity required to operate power equipment safely; ability to understand and follow verbal and/or written directions; ability to operate vehicles, including electric carts to carry, pick-up or deliver supplies to various work areas and/or campus locations. Ability to properly and continuously wear OSHA, ANSI, and WCU designated Personal Protective Equipment (PPE). WORKING CONDITIONS: Both indoor and Outdoor  during all weather conditions including rain and extreme heat; exposure to sun for extended periods of time; work on slippery and/or uneven surfaces; work while using or wearing safety equipment such as respirators, protective gloves, steel toed footwear, face shields and goggles, spray and rain suits; exposure to dust, oil/grease, gasoline, diesel fuel, smoke and pollen, and/or hazardous materials such as pesticides, herbicides, solvents and other toxic chemicals and fumes; exposure to loud noise levels from equipment and vehicle operation; must work with and around extremely dangerous equipment and machinery with moving parts; work assignments may be scheduled at any campus location(s), day and/or evenings and weekends as needed to conduct campus activities.  Adheres to WCU and departmental dress code, appearance is neat, clean and professional ; properly wears WCU designated Facilities Staff uniform daily.  Attends Chapel, official University events, and athletic (home) games, in support of University sanctioned activities. Compliance with OSHA, ANSI and WCU safety requirements and procedures is a condition of employment. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/E66B3C1689D7CACD88837E5AD889588C/jobs/941042": {
      "title": "Building Mechanic/Plumber",
      "description": "Building Mechanic/Plumber You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Building Mechanic/Plumber Hattiesburg - Hattiesburg, MS 39401 Apply Apply Description Job Summary Under the direction of the Maintenance Supervisor, and/or the Facilities Manager, a general Building Mechanic will perform a variety of skilled general building and equipment maintenance work related to plumbing, electrical, HVAC, locksmithing, carpentry, and painting as well as maintaining facilities in a safe, secure, and comfortable condition. This building mechanic position will also be responsible for the plumbing needs at William Carey University. The Plumber will provide guidance to other Building Mechanics as it relates to plumbing issues across campus and lead during any major plumbing projects. Duties and Responsibilities This job description does not state or imply that these are the only duties to be performed by the employee occupying this position.  Duties and responsibilities listed are essential job functions and exclude functions which are incidental to the performance of fundamental job duties: Responsibilities – Plumber: Install, maintain, repair, or replace plumbing fixtures, pipes and flushing mechanisms, pumps and motors, water faucets, valves, drinking fountains, fittings, gages and gaskets. Utilize appropriate tools to clean and clear clogged drains, repair damaged, broken and obstructed sewer lines.  Inspect, service and maintain Backflow Prevention Devices. Maintain, service and repair decorative fountains and water features. Responsibilities – Building Mechanic: Assist the university in implementing the statement of purpose. Assist the university in implementing the long-range institutional plan. Perform repair, installation, and troubleshooting of facility electrical systems, i.e. ballasts, relays, motors, controllers, and lighting. Remodel offices and classrooms, design, fabricate, install, and modify shelves, partitions, and counters; repair broken or damaged furniture; replace carpets, damaged floors, ceiling tiles, hand shades, bulletin boards, chalk boards, pictures and plaques. Inspect and repair roof leaks; clear gutter and downspout; install flashing, weather-stripping, gutters, downspout, and roof drains. Reset and adjust time clocks controlling automatic, lighting, heating, and air conditioning. Perform basic maintenance and repairs on various types of heating and ventilation equipment in the absence of the HVAC technician and when emergencies occur. Perform general painting; sand and repair walls; stucco, wall coverings; mix and apply paints and wood finishes, stains, and sealers. Maintain safe facilities; respond to water leaks, broken glass, gas leaks, fire, and other hazards. Confer with contractors and vendors performing contracted services. Perform duties and activities related to general locksmithing: install-maintain-repair-replace facility locksets, door hardware, etc. Perform emergency callback services to include weekends, holidays and nighttime hours as required and assigned. Perform other job-related duties as assigned. Qualifications Required Qualifications Three years (minimum) direct Journeyman Level plumbing experience. Valid Mississippi driver license with clear driving history. Ability to perform basic and advanced math calculations as it relates to plumbing and maintenance. Ability to read, write, and speak the English language. Must be able to perform duties in an on-campus setting. Preferred Qualifications High School diploma Previous employment/experience with Licensed/Mechanical – Plumbing Contractor desirable. Completion of formal Plumbing Course, with (Journeyman) Certification Successful completion of an accredited and recognized Building maintenance course. Backflow Device Inspection-Repair Certification Physical Demands Heavy physical labor with constant standing and walking for extended periods of time; walking over rough or uneven surfaces; frequent lifting, carrying, pushing and pulling of objects weighing up to fifty pounds; frequent bending, kneeling and stooping; manual dexterity required to climb ladders and operate power equipment safely; ability to operate vehicles including electric carts to carry, pick-up or deliver supplies to various work areas and/or campus locations.  Continuous wear of OSHA prescribed Personal Protective Equipment (PPE); Steel Toed Work boots, Eye Protection, Work Gloves. WORKING CONDITIONS: Indoor and outdoor environments in all weather conditions including rain, cold,  and extreme heat; exposure to sun for extended periods of time; work on slippery and/or uneven surfaces; work at above ground locations such as ceilings and roofs and in confined and/or awkwardly configured areas; work in poorly-lighted areas, and around electrical panels; work while using and wearing safety equipment; respirators, protective gloves, work boots/ steel toed footwear , face shields and goggles, hearing protection, and rain suits; exposure to dust, oil/grease, gasoline, diesel fuel, smoke and pollen, and/or materials such as solvents and other chemicals and fumes; exposure to loud noise levels from equipment and vehicle operation; must work with and around equipment and machinery with moving parts; work assignments may be scheduled at any campus location(s), day and/or evenings, holidays and weekends as needed to conduct maintenance activities. Adheres to WCU and departmental dress code; appearance is neat, clean and professional , properly wears WCU designated Facilities Staff uniform daily, without alteration or decoration.  Attends Chapel, official University events, and athletic (home) games, in support of University sanctioned activities. Compliance with established safety requirements and procedures is a condition of employment.  Adheres to the University Code of Conduct, and the policies and procedures as stated in the Administrative Staff and employee Handbook, and Facilities Departmental Handbook. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/E66B3C1689D7CACD88837E5AD889588C/jobs/941020": {
      "title": "Undergraduate Recruiter",
      "description": "Undergraduate Recruiter You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Undergraduate Recruiter Hattiesburg - Hattiesburg, MS 39401 Apply Apply Description Job Summary The Undergraduate Recruiter for the Hattiesburg Campus represents the university through outreach, engagement, and relationship-building within an assigned territory while establishing connections with high school and transfer students who are interested in attending WCU. Assisting the Admissions staff, the Recruiter also guides prospective students through the admissions process until their initial registration. The Undergraduate Recruiter manages a travel schedule, helps implement campus visits and events, and maintains relationships with high school and college representatives and organizations. Duties and Responsibilities This job description does not state or imply that these are the only duties to be performed by the employee occupying this position. Duties and responsibilities listed are essential job functions and exclude functions which are incidental to the performance of fundamental job duties. Assist the university in implementing the Statement of Purpose. Assist the university in implementing the long-range institutional and financial plans. Recruit students in assigned territory as assigned by the Director of Recruitment. Represent WCU at in-person and virtual high school and community college events as well as university sponsored and community events. Cultivate and maintain relationships with high school and community college counselors. Engage with potential students and WCU applicants regularly (phone, email, mail, text), and serve as a point of connection for students from the moment of interest until they enroll for classes. Host individual and group campus visits. Maintain a student correspondence file through Target X. Manage a travel schedule and maintain assigned vehicle. Assist in executing events sponsored by the Recruiting Department. Participate in the annual evaluation of the effectiveness of the Recruiting Department Perform other job-related tasks as deemed necessary for operation of the Recruiting Department and as assigned by the Director of Recruitment. Qualifications Required Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree Excellent customer service skills U.S. driver’s license, auto insurance and a clean driving history Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree from WCU Prior recruitment experience Prior CRM experience Prior computer experience Experience in Microsoft Office Suite Physical Demands Must possess mobility to work in a standard office setting, and to use standard office equipment, including a computer. Must have vision to read printed materials and a computer screen; hearing and speech to communicate in person and over the telephone. Must have the ability to sit for extended periods of time. Must have the ability to stand for extended periods of time. Must have strength and agility to move files, paper boxes, minor office equipment, recruitment supplies and setup equipment Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/E66B3C1689D7CACD88837E5AD889588C/jobs/953856": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant and Coordinator for the Registrar at Baton Rouge",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant and Coordinator for the Registrar at Baton Rouge You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Administrative Assistant and Coordinator for the Registrar at Baton Rouge Baton Rouge - Baton Rouge, LA 70806 Apply Apply Description Job Summary Under the direction of the Campus Director, the Administrative Assistant and Coordinator to the Registrar provides administrative, clerical, and student services support for the School of Nursing and, as needed, the College of Health Sciences. The position serves as a resource for students, faculty, staff, and the public; assists with registration and academic records processes; coordinates student-related documentation and data entry; and supports functions related to degree applications, VA certification, and registrar operations to ensure efficient and accurate service delivery. Duties and Responsibilities This job description does not state or imply that these are the only duties to be performed by the employee occupying this position.  Duties and responsibilities listed are essential job functions and exclude functions which are incidental to the performance of fundamental job duties. All duties and responsibilities listed below should be performed in an effective and efficient manner. Assist the university in implementing the Statement of Purpose Assist the university in implementing the long-range institutional and financial plans Serve as a primary point of contact for students, faculty, staff, and visitors by greeting guests, responding to in-person, telephone, voicemail, and email inquiries, distributing mail, and providing information regarding registration, Veteran Affairs benefits, and university processes. Support Registrar's Office operations by assisting with student registration, maintaining student records, processing academic documentation, providing required forms and guidance, entering data into student information systems, and serving as a liaison between the Baton Rouge campus and the Hattiesburg/Tradition Registrar's Offices. Assist the Registrar and Admissions staff in coordinating enrollment-related activities and guiding students through the admission, registration, and matriculation processes to ensure a seamless student experience. Assist with the planning, implementation, and administration of registration activities, orientations, commencement-related functions, recruitment initiatives, and other student engagement events for the School of Nursing and College of Health Sciences. Maintain and organize student, faculty, and departmental records, files, forms, applications, and program materials to ensure accuracy, accessibility, confidentiality, and compliance with university policies. Coordinate the preparation, production, and distribution of reports, correspondence, meeting minutes, admissions materials, orientation resources, and other departmental communications. Provide administrative support for faculty, staff, and departmental meetings, including scheduling, agenda preparation, room arrangements, and recording and distributing meeting minutes. Assist with recruitment and enrollment efforts for all School of Nursing and College of Health Sciences programs, including tracking and organizing program applications. Prepare, process, and maintain departmental financial and administrative records, including purchasing card documentation, purchase orders, check requests, mileage reimbursements, and related reports. Support academic and operational activities by assisting with exam proctoring, printing and publication requests, fingerprinting requirements, special projects, and other departmental initiatives. Maintain effective working relationships with university personnel, students, community partners, and external constituents while providing exceptional customer service. Supervise assigned work-study students and assist in training and monitoring their work performance. Maintain a clean, organized, and professional office environment. Coordinate with Information Technology to provide support to the Baton Rouge students, faculty, and staff and act as a liaison when needed Provide support for Field Services issues as needed and assigned Provide IT support for Baton Rouge campus events Perform other job related duties as assigned. Qualifications Required Qualifications High school diploma Prior experience with information technology Ability to use common office productivity software, including Microsoft Office suite (Word, Excel, and Outlook). Ability to learn WCU’s student database software Ability to simultaneously handle multiple tasks, solve practical problems and deal with a variety of situations and people Ability to respect and adhere to the strict confidentiality requirements Ability to make mathematical computations quickly and accurately Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in business or related field from a regionally accredited institution. Work experience in higher education Active Commission as a Louisiana Public Notary Physical Demands Must possess mobility to work in a standard office setting, and to use standard office equipment including a phone and computer Must have vision to read printed materials and a computer screen; hearing and speech to effectively communicate in person and over the telephone Must have the ability to sit or stand for extended periods of time (up to 4 hours consistently) Must have strength and agility to move files and minor office equipment. Must have ability and stamina to accompany students and paperwork to and from Student Services. Must be able to work required schedule in an on campus setting environment Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/E66B3C1689D7CACD88837E5AD889588C/jobs/957161": {
      "title": "Academic Records Specialist and Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Academic Records Specialist and Administrative Assistant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Academic Records Specialist and Administrative Assistant Hattiesburg - Hattiesburg, MS 39401 Apply Apply Description Job Summary Under the supervision of the Registrar, this position provides administrative and customer service support for the Registrar's Office. The Academic Records Specialist and Administrative Assistant serves as a primary point of contact for students, faculty, staff, and the public, assisting with registration, records management, academic data maintenance, and student information services. The position assists with ensuring accurate processing of student records while maintaining compliance with FERPA regulations, university policies, and established office procedures. Duties and Responsibilities This job description does not state or imply that these are the only duties to be performed by the employee occupying this position.  Duties and responsibilities listed are essential job functions and exclude functions which are incidental to the performance of fundamental job duties. Assist the university in implementing the statement of purpose. Assist the university in implementing the institutional and financial plan. Receive and perform general instruction from the Registrar. Serve as primary contact for students, faculty, staff, and the general public at the counter, over the telephone, and in the general Registrar’s Office email. Reply timely to inquiries (by phone, in person, and by email), select relevant data from a variety of sources and direct inquiries to appropriate person and/or unit. Assist with registration, add/drops, and updates of student information in Student Information System (SIS). Analyze day-to-day practices of workflow systems and best practice standards to create and revise streamlined processes. Maintain a high level of confidentiality and tactfulness in accordance with FERPA requirements and university policy. Update student information in SIS as directed by the Registrar. Manage office calendar of events and deadlines Assist with Commencement ceremonies and with any assigned corresponding processes. Assist Registrar’s office staff during peak times, i.e.  transcript ordering system and other areas as directed by the Registrar Perform back-up duties as assigned by the Registrar Assist with processing CLEP/AP/IB scores as needed Performs other job-related duties as assigned. Qualifications Required Qualifications High School diploma Ability to use common office software, including Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, and Outlook), TEAMS, Machforms, etc. Ability to learn WCU’s student database system in depth. Ability to communicate effectively, both verbal and written. Excellent interpersonal and organization skills.  Must always present a professional and respectful manner when dealing with a variety of situations and people. Superior work ethic and ability to exercise good judgment, demonstrate tactfulness and discretion at all times, and maintain confidentiality. Ability to respect the relationship between the Registrar’s Office functions and their effect on the job functions of other departments. Ability to multi-task, complete multiple assignments, work independently, as well as with others, possess a team player approach, and solve problems.  Must have a high attention to detail and accuracy, and ability to meet deadlines and establish priorities. Must be punctual, regular in attendance and able to work required hours in an on-campus setting. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree High level of technical proficiency Physical Demands Must possess mobility to work in a standard office setting, and to use standard office equipment, including a computer, calculator, copier, and scanner. Must have vision to read printed materials and a computer screen; hearing and speech to communicate in person and over the telephone. Must have the ability to sit for extended periods of time. Must have the strength and agility to move files, boxes, and minor equipment. Must have the ability to lift and carry up to 25 pounds to assist with commencement events. Must be able to transport mail to and from the office as needed. Must be able to perform duties in an on-campus setting Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/E66B3C1689D7CACD88837E5AD889588C/jobs/962823": {
      "title": "Assistant to the Registrar and Curriculum Management Coordinator",
      "description": "Assistant to the Registrar and Curriculum Management Coordinator You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant to the Registrar and Curriculum Management Coordinator Hattiesburg - Hattiesburg, MS 39401 Apply Apply Description Job Summary: Under the direction of the Registrar, the Assistant to the Registrar – Curriculum Management Coordinator provides administrative and operational support for Registrar's Office functions, with primary responsibility for curriculum management processes, academic records administration, and related student services. The position collaborates with faculty, academic departments, and university offices to ensure the accuracy and integrity of curricular information while maintaining compliance with FERPA and institutional policies. Duties and Responsibilities: This job description does not state or imply that these are the only duties performed by the employee occupying this position.  The duties and responsibilities listed are essential job functions and exclude functions that are incidental to fundamental job duties' performance. Assists the university in implementing the statement of purpose. Assists the university in implementing the institutional and financial plan. Maintain a thorough understanding of academic policies and procedures as related to higher education policy and curriculum management. Oversee the coordination of the academic curriculum process, timeline, schedule, and CIP assignment. Ensure university policies are met, and that accreditation and federal guidelines are followed. Collaborate with undergrad and graduate Curriculum Committee chairs and troubleshoot issues related to curriculum programs. Track course and curriculum approval process to stay on track. Provide oversight to academic departments in the creation of new academic programs. Coordinate the permanent database for all curricular/course approvals and changes, activate majors and minors to post historical degree(s) and create status/program as directed by the Registrar. Coordinate the revision of catalogs ensuring approved curriculum changes are included. Oversee university articulation agreements to ensure compliance with university policy. Manage the academic and the operating calendars for the Registrar’s Office. Prep and recommend decisions on student academic standing at end of each term. Manage office statistics and logbooks. Process Directed Studies and Independent Studies courses and determine the need for permanent status. Lead and co-coordinate attendance/participation and final grade process. Collaborate with academic units, Admission, Financial Aid, Business Office, and IT to troubleshoot registration related issues to ensure accurate student information. Revise the curriculum, calendar, and catalog sections of the office manual as updates are made. Coordinate training in curriculum proposals and new courses for campus units. Prep and compile academic records for reports as requested by the Registrar. Serve as a resource for Registrar’s Office technologies, forms, registration processes, and website information, and provide cross-functional support to ensure continuity of operations during staff absences or peak periods. Assist in graduation ceremonies and registration activities. Serve an active role within the Registrar team to achieve strategic goals of the unit and the institution. Assist in evaluating the effectiveness of the Registrar's Office to make improvements. Perform other job-related duties as assigned. Qualifications Required Qualifications Associates Degree Ability to use common office productivity software, Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, and Outlook), TEAMS, Machforms, Canvas, and the Student Portal . Strong verbal and written communication skills with the ability to interact effectively and professionally with students, faculty, staff, and the public. Demonstrated ability to exercise sound judgement, maintain confidentiality, and handle sensitive information in accordance with FERPA and university policies. Ability to manage multiple priorities, work independently and collaboratively, and adapt to changing deadlines and operational needs. Strong problem-solving, analytical, and critical thinking skills, with the ability to interpret and apply institutional policies, procedures , and regulatory requirements. Must be punctual and regular in attendance Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree Experience working in a higher education setting, particularly a Registrar’s Office. Experience with curriculum evaluation, data query software, file management, analysis and retrieval. Experience with web-based network technology and internet-based data collections. Experience training other professionals. High level of technical proficiency Physical Demands Must possess mobility to work in a standard office setting, use technology to meet needs. Must have vision to read printed materials and a computer screen, hearing and speech to communicate in person and over the telephone. Must have the ability to sit or stand for extended periods. Must have strength and agility to move minor office equipment. Must be able to work required schedule in an on -campus setting. Must be able to work limited evening and weekend work around graduations. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/E66B3C1689D7CACD88837E5AD889588C/jobs/874582": {
      "title": "Faculty for Preclinical Sciences",
      "description": "Faculty for Preclinical Sciences You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Faculty for Preclinical Sciences Hattiesburg - Hattiesburg, MS 39401 Apply Apply Description Job Summary Under the respective course director(s) and the Associate Dean, Preclinical Sciences, the successful candidate will provide instruction in the preclinical sciences, including the areas of microbiology, biochemistry, histology, embryology, and neurosciences.  The candidate will have administrative responsibilities commensurate with rank. Duties and Responsibilities This job description does not state or imply that these are the only duties to be performed by the employee occupying this position.  Duties and responsibilities listed are essential job functions and exclude functions, which are incidental to the performance of fundamental job duties. Assist WCUCOM and WCU in the implementation of their respective Mission Statements, Statement(s) of Purpose, Institutional Plan(s), and Financial Plan(s) Complete assigned tasks and participate in assigned work groups for preparing accreditation documents for all accrediting bodies Work with Course Directors and Associate Deans to integrate and implement WCUCOM courses into a four-year, seamless curriculum using on-site, distance-learning, and other standard and emerging standards Review relevant WCUCOM curriculum in its entirety and recommend pertinent suggestions to the Course Director(s) and Associate Dean, Preclinical Sciences Assist in monitoring the progress of all students to ensure successful progress toward graduation and recommend disciplinary action when necessary Teach in assigned courses Utilize course management software/distance learning technologies Make contributions to the advancement of knowledge and the development of osteopathic medicine through scientific research and community service Serve on assigned WCUCOM committees Assist in the interview process of prospective students Assist in student remediation as necessary and as recommended by the Promotion and Matriculation Committee Assist in the interview process for prospective incoming faculty Other job-related duties as assigned by the Course Director(s); Associate Dean, Preclinical Sciences; and WCUCOM Dean Qualifications Required Qualifications Have a terminal degree (PhD, DO, MD), or equivalent Have academic experience in microbiology, histology, embryology, neuroscience, and/or neuroanatomy Have excellent verbal and written communication skills Have experience with Microsoft Office Suite products Be able to complete multiple assignments, meet deadlines, and exercise good judgment Preferred Qualifications Experience in teaching and research in a COCA-accredited osteopathic medical school or college Experience in more than one preclinical (biomedical/preclinical/basic science) discipline Experience in course development and curriculum integration Physical Demands Possess the mobility to work in a standard classroom and/or office setting Have the vision to read printed materials and a computer screen; hearing and speech to communicate in person and over the telephone The ability to sit for extended periods of time Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/E66B3C1689D7CACD88837E5AD889588C/jobs/972400": {
      "title": "Housekeeper",
      "description": "Housekeeper You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Housekeeper Tradition - Biloxi, MS 39532 Apply Apply Description Job Summary Under the direction of the Housekeeping Supervisor or other assigned supervisor, maintains an assigned group of classrooms, rest rooms, offices, dormitories, houses and other facilities in a clean and orderly manner; perform a variety of diverse duties in cleaning and maintaining facilities.  Work is subject to general supervision by the Housekeeping Supervisor or other assigned Supervisor and is reviewed by general inspection and observation of results. Duties and Responsibilities This job description does not state or imply that these are the only duties to be performed by the employee occupying this position.  Duties and responsibilities listed are essential job functions and exclude functions which are incidental to the performance of fundamental job duties. Assist the university in implementing the statement of purpose Assist the university in implementing the long-range institutional plan Sweep, scrub, mop, and wax floors; vacuum and shampoo rugs and carpets in classrooms, offices, corridors, assembly areas, workshops and other areas; wash windows, chalkboards and walls; strip, wax and buff floors. Clean, dust and polish furniture, woodwork, desks, windowsills, etc. Empty and clean waste receptacles and pencil sharpeners; pick up paper; pick up trash containers and empty. Clean and sanitize rest rooms; floors, ceilings, walls, doors and hardware, fixtures, appliances and mirrors; restock supplies; polish metal fixtures. Move furniture and equipment; set up rooms for special events and meetings. Clean and adjust shades and blinds; adjust desks and other furniture; report other repair and maintenance needs and assist others in making repairs as required. Turn lights on and off; unlock and lock doors. Clean drinking fountains; make emergency clean-ups throughout facilities. Operate campus vehicles to pick up or deliver supplies as directed. Maintain inventory of cleaning supplies and materials and notifies supervisor when additional supplies and materials are needed. Notifies Maintenance Dispatcher of needed building repairs. Cleans dormitory public areas, and individual rooms as requested. Sets-up and takes down campus events, tables, chairs, electrical apparatus’, tents, etc., when assigned to Event Crew. Perform all other duties as assigned. Physical Demands Moderate physical labor including frequent lifting, carrying, reaching, pushing and pulling of objects weighing up to 50 pounds; frequent to constant walking, standing, bending, climbing and descending stairs or ladders, kneeling and stooping while cleaning, moving furniture or equipment, etc.; repetitive use of upper extremities on a regular basis; ability to operate electric or gasoline powered cart to travel and/or pick-up/deliver supplies to a variety of locations on campus; subject to occasional travel to various locations and campuses’ to work. Adheres to university dress code. Ability to properly and continuously wear OSHA, ANSI, and WCU designated Personal Protective Equipment (PPE). WORKING CONDITIONS : Primarily works in indoor environment with limited exposure to inclement weather during travel to and from assigned work areas; exposure to fumes from commercial cleaning products and noise from vacuums and other cleaning equipment; ability to work at any location during day, night, and evening hours including holidays, weekends, and on an as-needed basis. Adheres to WCU and departmental dress code, appearance is professional, neat, and clean; properly wears WCU designated Facilities Housekeeping Staff uniform daily, without added accessories, decoration or alterations.  Attends Chapel, official University events, and athletic (home) games, in support of university sanctioned activities. Ability to properly and continuously wear OSHA, ANSI and WCU prescribed occupational personal protective equipment (PPE).  Compliance with WCU Staff Handbook, Department Handbook and established WCU and OSHA safety requirements and procedures is a condition of employment. Qualifications Required Qualifications Ability to fluently read, write and speak English language. Ability to perform basic math calculations necessary to properly mix cleaning chemicals and supplies. Operate various powered equipment (i.e., mechanical scrubbers, polishers, buffers, washers, blowers, etc.) in performance of assigned duties. Accomplishes simple non-skilled maintenance to area and equipment. Must be able to perform duties in an on-campus setting. Preferred Qualifications High School diploma desirable. Two years of professional experience in janitorial, custodial, housekeeping or related work in a commercial institution or public or private building. Valid Mississippi driver license. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
